- Other business expenses: $950
- Net Schedule C profit ≈ $6,197
- SE tax (approx) ≈ $876 → half SE deduction ≈ $438
- Total income for MAGI calc: W‑2 64,800 + interest 1,770 + net business 6,197 = 72,767
- After half‑SE deduction MAGI ≈ 72,329 → below $75k, so you’d likely get the full student loan deduction (up to $2,500). Net effect: favorable to use actual method.

Scenario B — $950 are unreimbursed employee expenses (non‑deductible) and use simplified home office:
- Business gross: $11,200
- Home‑office (simplified): $700
- Net Schedule C profit = $10,500
