a) Simplified method: $5.00 × 140 sq ft = $700 deduction (no Form 8829).
b) Actual method (allocate rent): 16.47% × $24,600 ≈ $4,053 deduction (you can also allocate a portion of utilities, renter’s insurance, etc. — that will increase the deduction slightly if you have those bills and corroborating records). To use actual you report on Schedule C and complete Form 8829.

Because $4,053 (actual) > $700 (simplified) the actual method generally yields a bigger tax benefit if you have good records.

3) Self‑employment tax and related adjustment
- Schedule C net profit = $11,200 minus allowable business expenses (home office + other business expenses).
