- Business expenses = $4,053 (home office actual) + $950 = $5,003
- Net Schedule C profit = $11,200 − $5,003 = $6,197
- Self‑employment net for SE tax = 92.35% × $6,197 ≈ $5,723
- Self‑employment tax ≈ 15.3% × $5,723 ≈ $876
- You can deduct half of SE tax as an adjustment to income ≈ $438

