- Adjustments (above‑the‑line): half SE tax ≈ 438, student loan interest deduction ≈ 2,500
- AGI ≈ 72,767 − 438 − 2,500 = 69,829
- Standard deduction (HOH) = 20,800 → taxable income before QBI ≈ 49,029
- QBI deduction ≈ 1,239 → taxable income after QBI ≈ 47,790
These are approximate — final tax owed depends on tax brackets, credits, withholding, state tax, and exact rounding.

Forms you will likely need (federal)
- Form 1040
- Schedule 1 (additional income and adjustments) — although some items flow automatically from schedules
- Schedule C (Profit or Loss from Business) — report the $11,200 and your business expenses
- Schedule SE (Self‑Employment Tax)
- Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) if you use the regular method for the home‑office deduction. If you use the simplified method, you generally do not file Form 8829 — put the simplified deduction directly on Schedule C.
- Form 8995 (or 8995‑A) to claim the QBI deduction (likely Form 8995, the simpler form, if your taxable income is below the threshold)
